cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenGenesis-BioCore in your research, please cite this software."
title: "OpenGenesis-BioCore"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-18

authors:
  - family-names: "Çelik"
    given-names: "Recep"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2939-1009"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  OpenGenesis-BioCore is a local-first and extensible bioinformatics platform
  for reproducible biological data analysis. It provides a C++20 core,
  localhost browser interface, SQLite-backed project persistence, native
  worker and plugin execution, reproducible pipeline snapshots, durable
  artifacts, and integrated FASTA/FASTQ-to-variant-analysis workflows.

keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - reproducible workflows
  - local-first
  - genomics
  - FASTA
  - FASTQ
  - variant calling
  - C++20
  - scientific software
